comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-04T16:26:07.452Z","harness:codex","Duplicate-check evidence: complete all-status searches for jscpd 5.1.2 found closed prior refresh pm-ur4swu but no current patch owner. Registry jscpd 5.1.2 requires Node >=18 and was published 2026-09-03, compatible with pm-cli Node >=22.18.0. The same live census assigned Vitest 5 to pm-fokyhh, npm-package-arg 14 to pm-ksr40d, and TypeScript 7 to pm-do5b."
  "2026-09-04T16:43:08.481Z","harness:codex","Final implementation evidence: package.json and pnpm-lock.yaml resolve jscpd 5.1.2 including the new linux-arm64-musl artifact. Both jscpd configurations report zero clones across 1,167 repository files and 458 source files. Typecheck and pnpm audit pass with zero known vulnerabilities. Base package gate passes at 19,961,138 / 20,000,000 bytes and 1,423 files with no source maps. Fresh exact coverage passes 603 files / 8,364 tests at 61,894/61,894 statements, 46,879/46,879 branches, 12,871/12,871 functions, and 59,551/59,551 lines. Direct tracker-aware pnpm quality:static passes every repository, SDK, token, graph, and append-only history gate. Isolated packed npx and bunx smoke passes all 13 packages."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-04T16:43:09.081Z","harness:codex","Dependency freshness is a compatibility census, not a blind latest-version operation: patch updates can ship immediately when runtime and supply-chain contracts fit, while each incompatible major needs one canonical unclaimed owner with the exact external peer or engine blocker."
